// PARAM: --analysis interval
// The narrowing half of the Amato-Scozzari nested2 example, isolated from the
// endless outer loop that makes the full example's claim false under
// wraparound (soundness/01-nested2_endless_counter_wraps.vimp).
//
// What nested2 is actually about is this: the head widens j to [0,+inf], the
// guard narrows it back to [0,10], and the exit edge leaves j = [10,10]
// exactly rather than [0,10]. The step that follows is then 11 - j = 1 and
// not [1,11]. Without the endless loop around it nothing wraps, so the
// property is decidable and stays a precision case.
//
// Kept because the full example no longer checks it: its only check became
// UNKNOWN when the counter's wraparound made the outer claim false, which
// would otherwise have left the narrowing untested by anything.
void main() {
  int32 j, k;
  j := 0;
  while (j < 10) {
    j := j + 1
  };
  k := 11 - j;
  __voblint_check(j == 10);  // PROVED
  __voblint_check(k == 1)    // PROVED
}
